  "id": "pathological-aggression",
  "term": "pathological aggression",
  "definition": "Pathological aggression is aggression occurring in clinical or patient populations, rather than the normal range of aggressive traits seen in healthy people. In biological research, it has been associated with altered functional and structural connectivity between the orbitofrontal cortex and the amygdala.",
